option.END_PRECESSION_MINUTES.comment=Time for the ring axis to precess once; islands and shepherd bodies retain independent orbital periods.
option.WATER_WAVES=Water Waves
option.WATER_WAVE_QUALITY=Wave Detail Quality
option.WATER_WAVE_QUALITY.comment=Surface normals use 4/5/6 analytic layers. Low omits two fine ripples, medium omits the finest; both crest layers keep their amplitude and motion. Omitted mean slope enters above-water roughness. The underwater ITT collision field, eight-point integration and separate overworld underwater interface normals stay independent.
value.WATER_WAVE_QUALITY.0=Low (4 layers)
value.WATER_WAVE_QUALITY.1=Medium (5 layers)
value.WATER_WAVE_QUALITY.2=High (6 layers)
option.WATER_EFFECT_QUALITY=Water Reflection Quality
option.WATER_EFFECT_QUALITY.comment=Low/Balanced/High: enabled SSR uses at most 12/20/40 depth queries including refinement and 1/5/9 bilinear reflection footprints. Default SSR is off: sky reflections remain, scene-object reflections do not. Wave Detail Quality controls layers independently; no tier uses surface parallax. Underwater interfaces and refraction medium rejection stay. Low/balanced use sparse Nether rock tracing and lighter blur when SSR is enabled.
