option.SUNLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the strength of direct sunlight. 100 = default.
option.MOONLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the strength of moonlight at night. 100 = default.
option.SKYLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Determines the strength of directional ambient light from the sky.
option.MIN_AMBIENT.comment=Determines the ambient light floor in dark areas, so caves never go pitch black.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the strength of light emitted by torches, lava, glowstone and other light source blocks.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_SUPPRESSION.comment=Reduces daytime blocklight according to daylight and weather, preserving its original strength at night.
option.HANDHELD_LIGHTING.comment=Light-emitting items illuminate around the player with continuous distance falloff, including third person. Uses the brighter hand and caps the source before the strength multiplier. Daylight suppression remains.
option.HANDHELD_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the intensity of the handheld dynamic light.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH.comment=Enables lightning bolts lighting up the surroundings and the sky.
option.EMISSIVE_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the boost applied to emissive surfaces (glowstone, lava, portals...).
option.SHADOWS.comment=Master switch for the shadow map. §c[-]§r One of the most expensive features overall.
option.SHADOW_RESOLUTION.comment=Map side length: 1024, 1536 or 2048. Higher values reduce coarse edges and cost more. Overworld budget 1 caps at 1536; budget 2 at 1024; budget 0 uses the selection.
option.SHADOW_DISTANCE.comment=Shadow coverage in blocks. Greater distances cost more and spread the map pixels more thinly. Active overworld budgets cap coverage at 112 blocks.
option.ENTITY_SHADOW_DISTANCE.comment=Entity shadow range: 32 or 64 blocks. Active overworld budgets cap it at 32. Requires entity shadows.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Filter spread: 1, 2 or 4. Basic filtering does not expand; active overworld budgets cap the basis at 2. Native surfaces retain at least half the selected pixel spread; coarse distant shadows may soften further in world units.
option.COLORED_SHADOWS.comment=Enables tinted shadows cast by stained glass and water; clear glass casts none.
option.STATIC_SHADOW_FALLBACK.comment=Skylight-based approximation outside map coverage. Distance fade runs from 24 to 8 blocks inside the map boundary; ordinary underwater does not gain extra direct light.
option.SSS_FOLIAGE.comment=Enables leaves and plants to let some light through from behind.
option.SSS_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the intensity of the foliage translucency effect.
option.SKY_MODE.comment=Determines how the sky is rendered. The simple gradient is the fastest option.
option.SUN_MOON_MODE.comment=Determines the style of the sun and moon.
option.STARS.comment=Enables the Overworld galactic band and stars with subtle colour and twinkle. Star positions follow the sun and moon; the End uses a separate catalogue.
option.STAR_AMOUNT.comment=Sets the Overworld night star density. Normal is the default; dense settings fill more of the sky, also affecting fine stars in the galactic band without changing the End catalogue.
option.CLOUD_MODE.comment=Vanilla uses game cloud geometry; planar uses Astra cloud layers. Default high planar quality prioritizes clear edges and costs more than low quality.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=Determines the coverage of the planar cloud layer. §e[*]§r Only works when Clouds is set to the planar style.
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=Casts the moving planar cloud field onto the ground as travelling shade, in clear weather as well as in rain. §e[*]§r Only works when Clouds is set to the planar style. §c[-]§r Off in every profile; its strength and horizon fade still need in-game calibration.
option.AIR_PERSPECTIVE.comment=Enables a warm horizon tint toward the sun at sunrise/sunset, varying with view angle.
option.BIOME_TINT.comment=Adds subtle biome colour to thin atmospheric haze, fading with distance.
option.BIOME_TINT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the intensity of the biome tint.
option.WATER_WAVES.comment=Enables animated water surface normals.
option.WATER_WAVE_HEIGHT.comment=Determines water-wave amplitude when viewed from above or below the surface.
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED.comment=Determines water-surface flow speed when viewed from above or below the surface.
option.SCREENSPACE_REFLECTIONS.comment=Enables SSR on water, puddles and Nether rock. Water and puddle misses fall back to sky reflection; ice top faces retain environment reflection. §c[-]§r High cost when many reflective surfaces are on screen.
option.SCREENSPACE_REFRACTION.comment=Enables refraction under the water surface with per-tap depth and side rejection.
option.REFRACTION_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the distortion strength of the refracted background. Water depth does not amplify it further.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION.comment=Light attenuation over real water distance, including the underwater camera leg and surface transmission. 0 disables absorption; distance fog has its own control.
option.WATER_CHARACTER.comment=Water color by depth. Cold: blue from the shallows down. Balanced: cyan-green shallows fading to deep blue. Tropical: bright cyan shallows, blue depths.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment=Enables caustic light patterns on the seafloor, cast along with shadows and fading with depth.
option.UNDERWATER_PARTICLES.comment=Enables suspended particles inside water bodies; nearby thin waterfall sheets omit them.
option.FANCY_TRANSLUCENTS.comment=Enables premultiplied-alpha blending for water and translucent blocks; lets reflections and refraction mix freely.
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Adjusts the density of distance fog.
option.SKY_FOG_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts how much near/mid fog blends into the sky color. The far horizon always converges to sky.
option.BORDER_FOG.comment=Enables fog at loaded-world edges. In the current Nether model this also gates all air distance fog.
option.CAVE_FOG.comment=Enables extra fog in deep underground areas.
option.UNDERWATER_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Distance fog, default 35%, sharing the surface cyan palette and incident lighting. Weather changes illumination without a separate grey overlay. 0 disables fog; absorption remains independent.
option.NETHER_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Adjusts Nether distance-fog density and its saturation distance. Zero disables this fog layer; 70 is the default.
option.END_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Adjusts the density of the End void fog gradient.
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG.comment=Ray-marched overworld air replaces distance fog, rain haze and air godrays when enabled with nonzero density, including cave air. Blindness, lava, powder snow and underwater remain separate. Zero density restores the ordinary air path. Default off; independent of TAA.
option.VOLUME_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Sea-level volume density: higher values increase extinction, with thinner air high up and denser valleys. This height-based exponential model is not calibrated to equal the ordinary distance-fog curve.
option.NETHER_VOXEL_LIGHT.comment=Lets fire, soul fire and lava cast coloured light into the surrounding space, propagated 8 steps per frame across a 64-block volume. Voxel emitters retain their species colours independently of ordinary block-light tint controls. Requires Shadows and OpenGL 4.3 compute shaders.
option.TONEMAP_OPERATOR.comment=Chooses the tone curve. Overworld surface and ordinary underwater share it; underwater keeps fixed 1.6x exposure compensation plus manual exposure. End sky has its own display transform.
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Adjusts the overall brightness of the image.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=Smoothly adjusts exposure from scene brightness with a gain of 0.60 to 2.20. Darkening is faster than brightening. Applies in Overworld air and nearby thin waterfall sheets; water bodies, the Nether and the End keep manual exposure. Off by default; quality profiles preserve your choice.
option.SATURATION.comment=Adjusts overall colorfulness. 100 is neutral, including the fresh natural look.
option.VIBRANCE.comment=Adjusts the colorfulness of the image, but already colorful pixels are less affected.
option.CONTRAST.comment=100 is neutral. Fresh natural adjusts HDR luminance around 18% grey before tone mapping, preserving colour ratios. Original look, Nether and End retain display-space contrast.
option.COLOR_TEMPERATURE.comment=Adjusts the warm/cool balance of the image. Negative = cooler.
option.BLOOM.comment=Enables a soft glow around bright areas.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the intensity of the bloom.
option.GODRAYS.comment=Enables volumetric light shafts when looking at the sun/moon through gaps. §c[-]§r This effect can impact performance.
option.GODRAYS_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the intensity of the godrays.
option.GODRAYS_SUN_OCCLUSION.comment=Fades the light shafts by how much of the sun or moon disc real geometry covers; without it occlusion is decided only along each shaft's own march. §e[*]§r Needs Godrays enabled.
option.DITHERING.comment=Applies interleaved gradient noise on the output to remove banding. §e[*]§r Keep it on when no anti-aliasing is used.
option.VIGNETTE.comment=Darkens the corners of the screen.
option.WAVING_FOLIAGE.comment=Visible plants and their shadows share motion. Leaves fade out over 32-64 blocks; ground plants over 64-96 with a budget, otherwise 128-192.
option.WAVING_FOLIAGE_STRENGTH.comment=Motion amplitude, default 50%; 0 stops motion. Larger amplitudes may increase fine leaf-shadow shimmer.
option.VOXY_SUPPORT.comment=Reserved integration switch. Voxy distant-terrain rendering is not implemented; enabling this option has no rendering effect.
option.OVERWORLD_BUDGET.comment=Overworld only. 1 caps shadows at 1536/112, entities at 32 and fades water over 48-96 blocks; 2 caps shadows at 1024/112 and fades water over 32-64. Both use software shadow comparison and reduced distant detail. 0 uses raw options. Cloud quality is independent and uncapped by this budget. Caps never raise lighter settings or enable effects.

