profile.PERFORMANCE=§aPerformance
profile.BALANCED=§eBalanced (Default)
profile.QUALITY=§6Fine
profile.comment=Three tiers. Balanced uses 1536/96 shadows and fixed 16-corner surface filtering, with object reflections, Bloom, underwater shafts and Nether voxel light off. Fine restores these effects with 2048/112 shadows. Colours remain independent; use the shadow toggle to disable real-time shadows.

option.UNDERWATER_LIGHT_SHAFTS=§eUnderwater Sun Shafts§r
option.UNDERWATER_LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment=Sun and moon light refracts through flowing surface waves, forming textured strands nearby and at medium distances, with a soft far fade. Clear days show more, stronger strands. §e[*]§r Requires Shadows and Water Waves; independent of Godrays in Post Processing.
option.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_STRENGTH=Underwater Shaft Strength
option.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the brightness of underwater sun shafts without changing underwater fog density.
option.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_DISTANCE=Near Shaft Fade Distance
option.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_DISTANCE.comment=Nearby shafts fade gently within this distance, in blocks. Default: 1 block. Larger values weaken nearby light; water and the light source determine shaft positions.
option.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_SAMPLES=§eUnderwater Shaft Detail§r
option.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_SAMPLES.comment=Adjusts underwater shaft and shadow detail (4-10). Higher values cost more GPU time; the lightweight overworld budget uses at most 7.
value.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_SAMPLES.4=Fast
value.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_SAMPLES.7=Balanced
value.UNDERWATER_SHAFT_SAMPLES.10=Fine
option.END_STONE_GLOW=End Stone Glow
option.END_STONE_GLOW.comment=Optional faint pore emission on End stone; disabled by default. Surface highlights are independent.
option.NETHERRACK_GLOW=Netherrack Reflections
option.NETHERRACK_GLOW.comment=Scales texture-driven reflections on Nether netherrack. Requires Screen-space Reflections; does not emit light.
option.DEBUG_VERTEX_AO=Vertex AO View
option.DEBUG_VERTEX_AO.comment=1 displays terrain AO directly (white=1). Requires SHADOWS.
option.DEBUG_DISABLE_WATER_ABSORPTION=Diagnostic: Disable Water Absorption
option.DEBUG_DISABLE_WATER_ABSORPTION.comment=Removes the per-channel extinction of the scene seen through water. Keeps the in-scatter medium, so a remaining tint can be attributed to the medium instead of absorption. Diagnostic switch; leave off for normal rendering.
option.DEBUG_DISABLE_UNDERWATER_FOG=Diagnostic: Disable Underwater Fog
option.DEBUG_DISABLE_UNDERWATER_FOG.comment=Removes the water in-scatter/fog term while keeping absorption, so depth attenuation stays visible without the medium's own colour. Diagnostic switch; leave off for normal rendering.
option.DEBUG_DISABLE_COLOR_GRADE=Diagnostic: Disable Color Grade
option.DEBUG_DISABLE_COLOR_GRADE.comment=Bypasses the display-space grade (temperature, vibrance, saturation, contrast, tonal balance). Exposure, the tone map, water and fog are unaffected. Diagnostic switch; leave off for normal rendering.

option.ANTIALIASING=Antialiasing
option.ANTIALIASING.comment=Off, spatial FXAA, or optional temporal TAA. TAA stabilizes static surfaces using HDR history; foliage uses previous-frame deformation, while entities, water and clouds use a conservative current-frame path. May soften detail. Presets keep Off or FXAA.
value.ANTIALIASING.0=Off
value.ANTIALIASING.1=FXAA
value.ANTIALIASING.2=TAA (optional)

option.DIRECTIONAL_SKYLIGHT=Directional Skylight
option.DIRECTIONAL_SKYLIGHT.comment=SH sky illumination for overworld air surfaces. Has no effect when sky ambient intensity is zero. Preserves cave fill and night vision. Independent of TAA and planar clouds. Combined with Ambient Contact Occlusion, the AO compose re-evaluates this term along the bent normal; without AO it keeps the geometric normal. Disabled by default.
option.SCREENSPACE_AO=Ambient Contact Occlusion
option.SCREENSPACE_AO.comment=Half-resolution overworld terrain AO, affecting ambient light only. Uses the stronger of vertex AO and screen AO. Requires real-time shadows for separate vertex AO; independent of TAA. Excludes underwater, foliage, entities and transparents. Combined with Directional Skylight, the ambient sky follows the AO bent normal and falls back to the geometric normal where no valid occlusion information exists.
option.AO_STRENGTH=Contact Occlusion Strength
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment=Affects ambient light only. Zero disables the screen AO stages.
option.AO_RADIUS=Contact Occlusion Radius
option.AO_RADIUS.comment=100 means one block. Screen-space depth cannot represent offscreen occluders.

