option.OVERWORLD_LOOK=Overworld look
option.OVERWORLD_LOOK.comment=Fresh natural balances warm daylight and blue ambient light without a fixed shadow lift or saturation boost. Uchimura compresses the colour as a whole; genuinely bright highlights gradually approach white. Saturation and contrast 100 are neutral. Twilight warmth and independent quality settings remain.
value.OVERWORLD_LOOK.0=Original palette
value.OVERWORLD_LOOK.1=Fresh natural (default)
option.COLOR_STYLE=Colour style
option.COLOR_STYLE.comment=Existing styles and RGB controls adjust the selected overworld look; quality changes preserve colours. Original look with Native style and 100% channels uses the original palette.
option.SHADOW_FILTER_QUALITY=Shadow filter quality
option.SHADOW_FILTER_QUALITY.comment=Native overworld surfaces: Basic uses 4 fixed corners; Soft and Wide both use four footprints, 16 corners. Wide spreads farther, not more samples. Distant support has a minimum spread and no frame-random jitter. Water and other dimensions use their own branches; budgets limit water filtering.
option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Sky and cloud quality
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=Low: quarter resolution, up to 12 coarse queries. Medium: half, up to 16. High: native resolution, four subpixel rays per pixel, integrated opacity at a target 4-block spacing with up to 512 segments. Reflections share high density integration. High preserves edge coverage without sharpening. Independent of the overworld budget; significantly more expensive.
option.VOLUME_FOG_QUALITY=Volumetric fog quality
option.VOLUME_FOG_QUALITY.comment=Low: quarter resolution / up to 12 steps; balanced: half / 24; high: half / 48. Adaptive sampling reduces short-ray counts; disabling it uses the selected fixed count. Only applies with volumetric fog enabled.
